        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We add two matrices by adding the corresponding entries. We can only do this if they have the same number of rows and columns, that is, they have the same dimensions.</p>",
            "readable_text": "We add two matrices by adding the corresponding entries. We can only do this if they have the same number of rows and columns, that is, they have the same dimensions.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, consider the matrices\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: [1|3; 2|4]]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, consider the matrices\n[MATH: [1|3; 2|4]]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We see that both <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: B]</span> are <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2\\times 2]</span> matrices, so we can add them. The sum <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {A} + {B}\\,]</span> is given by\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: A + B|= [1|3; 2|4] + [1|0; 0|\u2212 1]; = [1 + 1|3 + 0; 2 + 0|4 + (\u2212 1)]; = [2|3; 2|3].]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We see that both [MATH: A] and [MATH: B] are [MATH: 2\\times 2] matrices, so we can add them. The sum [MATH: {A} + {B}\\,] is given by\n[MATH: A + B|= [1|3; 2|4] + [1|0; 0|\u2212 1]; = [1 + 1|3 + 0; 2 + 0|4 + (\u2212 1)]; = [2|3; 2|3].]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>In general, the sum of two matrices is another matrix with the same dimensions.</p>",
            "readable_text": "In general, the sum of two matrices is another matrix with the same dimensions.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nWe add two matrices by adding the corresponding entries. We can only do this if they have the same number of rows and columns, that is, they have the same dimensions.\n\nContent:\nFor example, consider the matrices\n[MATH: [1|3; 2|4]]\n\nContent:\nWe see that both [MATH: A] and [MATH: B] are [MATH: 2\\times 2] matrices, so we can add them. The sum [MATH: {A} + {B}\\,] is given by\n[MATH: A + B|= [1|3; 2|4] + [1|0; 0|\u2212 1]; = [1 + 1|3 + 0; 2 + 0|4 + (\u2212 1)]; = [2|3; 2|3].]\n\nContent:\nIn general, the sum of two matrices is another matrix with the same dimensions."
      },
