          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We see that both <span class=\"math\">[MATH: A]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: B]</span> are <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2\\times 2]</span> matrices, so, we can subtract them. The difference <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {A} - {B}\\,]</span> is given by\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: A \u2212 B|= [1|3; 2|4] \u2212 [1|0; 0|\u2212 1]; = [1 \u2212 1|3 \u2212 0; 2 \u2212 0|4 \u2212 (\u2212 1)]; = [0|3; 2|5].]</span></p>",
