    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nWe add two matrices by adding the corresponding entries. We can only do this if they have the same number of rows and columns, that is, they have the same dimensions.\n\nContent:\nFor example, consider the matrices\n[MATH: [1|3; 2|4]]\n\nContent:\nWe see that both [MATH: A] and [MATH: B] are [MATH: 2\\times 2] matrices, so we can add them. The sum [MATH: {A} + {B}\\,] is given by\n[MATH: A + B|= [1|3; 2|4] + [1|0; 0|\u2212 1]; = [1 + 1|3 + 0; 2 + 0|4 + (\u2212 1)]; = [2|3; 2|3].]\n\nContent:\nIn general, the sum of two matrices is another matrix with the same dimensions.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Adding Square Matrices\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: A+B,] where\n\n[MATH: [1|\u2212 5; \u2212 2|3]]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe add the corresponding entries:\n\n[MATH: A + B|= [1|\u2212 5; \u2212 2|3] + [\u2212 10|2; 2|\u2212 4]; = [1 \u2212 10|\u2212 5 + 2; \u2212 2 + 2|3 \u2212 4]; = [\u2212 9|\u2212 3; 0|\u2212 1]]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: [\u2212 4|\u2212 5; 12|3] + [\u2212 9|5; 6|\u2212 11] =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [\u2212 13|\u2212 10; 12|\u2212 8]]\nb. [MATH: [\u2212 5|10; 18|\u2212 8]]\nc. [MATH: [\u2212 13|0; 18|\u2212 14]]\nd. [MATH: [\u2212 13|0; 18|\u2212 8]]\ne. [MATH: [\u2212 13|10; 18|\u2212 14]]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: A + B], where\n[MATH: A = [2|5; 3|1], B = [4|1; \u2212 2|2].]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [5|2; 1|3]]\nb. [MATH: [5|5; 5|5]]\nc. [MATH: [6|6; 1|3]]\nd. [MATH: [\u2212 6|6; 1|\u2212 3]]\ne. [MATH: [6|6; 6|6]]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Adding Non-Square Matrices\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: {A}+ {B},] where\n[MATH: [1|3|1|0; 2|4|\u2212 1|2]]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe add the corresponding entries:\n\n[MATH: A + B|= [1|3|1|0; 2|4|\u2212 1|2] + [\u2212 2|\u2212 3|1|1; 1|\u2212 2|3|1]; = [1 + (\u2212 2)|3 + (\u2212 3)|1 + 1|0 + 1; 2 + 1|4 + (\u2212 2)|\u2212 1 + 3|2 + 1]; = [\u2212 1|0|2|1; 3|2|2|3]]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: [2|\u2212 12; 7|\u2212 4; \u2212 8|7] + [3|0; \u2212 1|5; 9|13] =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [5|\u2212 12; 6|9; 1|\u2212 20]]\nb. [MATH: [5|\u2212 12; 8|1; 1|\u2212 20]]\nc. [MATH: [\u2212 5|\u2212 12; 6|1; 17|20]]\nd. [MATH: [5|\u2212 12; 6|1; 1|20]]\ne. [MATH: [5|12; \u2212 6|1; 1|20]]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: X + Y,] where\n\n[MATH: X = [2|\u2212 1|8; \u2212 14|0|\u2212 6], Y = [\u2212 12|3|5; 13|1|0].]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [\u2212 10|2|13; \u2212 1|1|\u2212 6]]\nb. [MATH: [10|2|13; \u2212 1|13|\u2212 6]]\nc. [MATH: [\u2212 10|\u2212 2|13; \u2212 1|13|\u2212 6]]\nd. [MATH: [\u2212 10|2|13; 1|13|\u2212 6]]\ne. [MATH: [\u2212 10|2|13; \u2212 1|13|6]]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Tutorial: Subtracting Matrices\n\nContent:\nWe can subtract matrices in the same way that we add matrices: we subtract the corresponding entries. Again, we can only do this if they have the same number of rows and columns, that is, they have the same dimensions.\n\nContent:\nFor example, consider the matrices\n[MATH: [1|3; 2|4]]\n\nContent:\nWe see that both [MATH: A] and [MATH: B] are [MATH: 2\\times 2] matrices, so, we can subtract them. The difference [MATH: {A} - {B}\\,] is given by\n[MATH: A \u2212 B|= [1|3; 2|4] \u2212 [1|0; 0|\u2212 1]; = [1 \u2212 1|3 \u2212 0; 2 \u2212 0|4 \u2212 (\u2212 1)]; = [0|3; 2|5].]\n\nContent:\nAgain, the difference of two matrices is another matrix with the same dimensions.\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Example: Subtracting Matrices\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: A-B,] where\n\n[MATH: [2|\u2212 1; \u2212 1|0; 3|2]]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe subtract the corresponding entries:\n\n[MATH: A \u2212 B|= [2|\u2212 1; \u2212 1|0; 3|2] \u2212 [0|\u2212 1; 2|\u2212 1; \u2212 1|3]; = [2 \u2212 0|\u2212 1 \u2212 (\u2212 1); \u2212 1 \u2212 2|0 \u2212 (\u2212 1); 3 \u2212 (\u2212 1)|2 \u2212 3]; = [2|0; \u2212 3|1; 4|\u2212 1]]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: [7|\u2212 4|9; 1|10|\u2212 7] \u2212 [\u2212 8|6|\u2212 2; \u2212 4|3|\u2212 6] =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [15|\u2212 2|11; 5|7|\u2212 1]]\nb. [MATH: [15|\u2212 10|11; \u2212 3|7|\u2212 1]]\nc. [MATH: [\u2212 1|\u2212 10|11; 5|7|\u2212 1]]\nd. [MATH: [15|\u2212 10|7; 5|7|\u2212 1]]\ne. [MATH: [15|\u2212 10|11; 5|7|\u2212 1]]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: P \u2212 Q], where\n[MATH: P = [4|3; 1|2], Q = [1|2; 3|4].]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [3|1; \u2212 2|\u2212 2]]\nb. [MATH: [3|1; 2|2]]\nc. [MATH: [\u2212 2|\u2212 2; 1|3]]\nd. [MATH: [2|2; \u2212 2|\u2212 2]]\ne. [MATH: [\u2212 2|\u2212 2; 3|1]]"
  }
